  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNODC-OHCHR PROMIS IV Cross-regional cooperation and extension to Mauritania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme aims to improve cross-regional cooperation between West and Central Africa and MENA and strengthen the capacities of Mauritania to develop a human rights-based and gender-sensitive response to smuggling of migrants and related crimes, including trafficking in persons, and to protect and promote the human rights of migrants on the migratory routes. The programme will: 1) Monitor and raise awareness of the human rights situation of migrants in vulnerable situations and strengthen legal and policy frameworks 2) Strengthen the the capacities of law enforcement and judicial actors in detecting, investigating and prosecuting TIP and SOM 3) Strengthen cross-regional and international judicial cooperation 4) Develop specific actions related to gender in the context of migration, trafficking in persons and smuggling of migrants</narrative>
  </description>
